<title>SWEDEN: BIATHLON-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BIATHLON-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>OSTERSUND, Sweden 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of World Cup</p>
<p>biathlon events on Thursday:</p>
<p>Men's 20 km</p>
<p>1. Wilfried Pallhuber (Italy) 50 minutes 46.7 seconds, two</p>
<p>penalty rounds</p>
<p>2. Vesa Hietalahti (Finland) 50:47.6 (1)</p>
<p>3. Pavel Muslimov (Russia) 51:01.1 (1)</p>
<p>4. Ricco Gross (Germany) 51:17.2 (1)</p>
<p>5. Alexei Kobelyev (Russia) 51:38.3 (2)</p>
<p>6. Herve Flandin (France) 51:38.8 (1)</p>
<p>7. Carsten Heymann (Germany) 51:49.9 (1)</p>
<p>8. Alexei Aidarov (Belorus) 51:58.9 (3)</p>
<p>9. Hubert Leitgeb (Italy) 52:11.3 (2)</p>
<p>10 Mikael Lofgren (Sweden) 52:16.9 (2).</p>
<p>World Cup standings.</p>
<p>1. Muslimov 64 points</p>
<p>2. Sven Fischer (Germany) 60</p>
<p>3. Viktor Maygorov (Russia) 52</p>
<p>4. Pavel Rostovtsev (Russia) 50</p>
<p>5. Frank Luck (Germany) 47.</p>
<p>Women's 15 km</p>
<p>1. Anna Volkova (Russia) 46:08.1 (1)</p>
<p>2. Shu Mei Yu (China) 47:25.4 (2)</p>
<p>3. Svetlana Paramyguina (Belorus) 47:35.2 (2)</p>
<p>4. Magdalena Forsberg (Sweden) 48:21.2 (3)</p>
<p>5. Kathi Sshwaab (Germany) 48:29.6 (2)</p>
<p>6. Tadeya Brankovic (Slovenia) 48:38.3 (2)</p>
<p>7. Olessia Toupilenko (Russia) 49:00.6 (1)</p>
<p>8. Annukka Mallat (Finland) 49:10.8 (1)</p>
<p>9. Petra Behle (Germany) 49:14.1 (3)</p>
<p>10. Mart Schwarzbacherova (Slovakia) 49:25.0 (1)</p>
<p>World Cup standings</p>
<p>1. Petra Behle (Germany) 68 points</p>
<p>2. Forsberg 66</p>
<p>3. Simone Greiner-Petter-Memm (Germany) 56</p>
